"overview": "Atrial fibrillation is the most common sustained cardiac arrhythmia. It is characterized by chaotic and disorganized electrical activity in the atria, resulting in an irregular and often rapid heartbeat. AFib increases the risk of stroke, heart failure, cardiomyopathy, and other cardiovascular complications.",

